Fix: give each hot variable its own cache line by padding the struct.

```c
struct Counters {
    long counterA;
    char pad[56];   // push counterB to the next 64B line
    long counterB;
};
```

- Pad to the cache line size (commonly 64 bytes) so each field lands on a separate line.
- Trades a little memory for no more false ping-pong between cores.
